{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>You shall not take up a vain report.</b> As the Targum renders: לָא תְקַבֵּל שְׁמַע דִשְׁקָר — a warning to one who accepts evil speech, and to a judge, that he not hear the words of one litigant until the other litigant comes (ibid.)." "<b>You shall not put your hand with the wicked.</b> One who brings a false claim against another — that you should assure him you will be a witness of violence for him."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:01.096520954Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}